[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2m------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "---\r\nname: tuistory\r\ndescription: Automate terminal TUI applications via virtual PTY using tuistory. Use for deterministic terminal automation, text snapshots, and .cast recordings. Examples: \"automate terminal app\", \"record terminal session\", \"tuistory capture\", \"virtual pty automation\", \"terminal regression test\"\r\n---\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;45mTuistory Driver\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe orchestrator routed you here. Use these mechanics to execute your plan.\r\n\r\nLaunch a target command in a virtual PTY with Playwright-style CLI for typing, pressing keys, waiting, snapshotting, and recording.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mWhen to use\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n • Routine TUI automation and regression checks\r\n • Deterministic \u001b[38;5;45mwait\u001b[0m / \u001b[38;5;45mwait-idle\u001b[0m against the virtual screen buffer\r\n • Text snapshots of exactly what the user would see\r\n • Any scenario where you do **not** need to prove real terminal keyboard encoding\r\n\r\nIf you need to prove what Ghostty or Kitty actually emits for a given keystroke, use **true-input** instead.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mPrerequisites\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n``\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\nnpm install -g tuistory    # or: bun add -g tuistory\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\nOptional: \u001b[0mtmux\u001b[38;5;45m (scrollback flows), \u001b[0masciinema\u001b[38;5;45m (recordings), \u001b[0magg\u001b[38;5;45m (\u001b[0m.cast\u001b[38;5;45m to \u001b[0m.gif\u001b[38;5;45m).\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mCore pattern\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\nTCTL=${PI_AGENT_CONTROL_ROOT}/bin/tctl\r\n\r\n$TCTL launch \"pi\" -s demo --backend tuistory \\\r\n  --repo-root /path/to/worktree \\\r\n  --cols 120 --rows 36 \\\r\n  --env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\r\n$TCTL -s demo wait \">\" --timeout 15000\r\n$TCTL -s demo type \"hello\"\r\n$TCTL -s demo press enter\r\n$TCTL -s demo snapshot --trim\r\n$TCTL -s demo close\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\n**Note:** \u001b[0m--repo-root\u001b[38;5;45m is mandatory for \u001b[0mpi\u001b[38;5;45m launches — \u001b[0mtctl\u001b[38;5;45m enforces it.\r\n\r\n**Always pass \u001b[0m--env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\u001b[38;5;45m** when launching. The virtual PTY doesn't advertise color support, so Node.js apps (Ink/chalk) suppress all color escape codes without these.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mCommand reference (via tctl)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n| Command | Purpose |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| \u001b[0mlaunch <cmd> -s <name> --backend tuistory\u001b[38;5;45m | Start a tuistory session |\r\n| \u001b[0mtype <text>\u001b[38;5;45m | Send literal text |\r\n| \u001b[0mpress <key> [keys...]\u001b[38;5;45m | Send key chord (e.g., \u001b[0mpress shift enter\u001b[38;5;45m) |\r\n| \u001b[0mwait <pattern>\u001b[38;5;45m | Block until text or \u001b[0m/regex/\u001b[38;5;45m appears |\r\n| \u001b[0mwait-idle\u001b[38;5;45m | Block until output stabilizes |\r\n| \u001b[0msnapshot [--trim]\u001b[38;5;45m | Print cleaned text (\u001b[0m--trim\u001b[38;5;45m strips trailing blanks) |\r\n| \u001b[0mclose\u001b[38;5;45m | Tear down session |\r\n\r\nLaunch options: \u001b[0m--cols <n>\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--rows <n>\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--cwd <path>\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--env KEY=VALUE\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--record <path>\u001b[38;5;45m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mRecording\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nPass \u001b[0m--record\u001b[38;5;45m at launch. \u001b[0mtctl\u001b[38;5;45m wraps \u001b[0masciinema rec\u001b[38;5;45m around the PTY, so recording **must** be set at launch time (raw \u001b[0mtuistory\u001b[38;5;45m cannot record):\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\n$TCTL launch \"pi\" -s demo --backend tuistory \\\r\n  --repo-root /path/to/worktree \\\r\n  --cols 120 --rows 36 --record /tmp/demo.cast \\\r\n  --env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;45m... interact ...\u001b[0m\r\n$TCTL -s demo close    # finalizes the .cast\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\nBefore/after comparison -- launch two sessions against different worktrees:\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\n$TCTL launch \"pi\" -s before --backend tuistory \\\r\n  --repo-root /path/to/baseline-worktree \\\r\n  --cols 120 --rows 36 --record /tmp/before.cast \\\r\n  --env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\r\n\r\n$TCTL launch \"pi\" -s after --backend tuistory \\\r\n  --repo-root /path/to/candidate-worktree \\\r\n  --cols 120 --rows 36 --record /tmp/after.cast \\\r\n  --env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\nPlayback: \u001b[0masciinema play /tmp/demo.cast\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mtmux (scrollback flows only)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nOnly needed when the demo requires terminal-emulator scrollback and the app uses the standard buffer (not alternat"]
[0.000, "o", "e screen). True-input sessions rarely need tmux because the real terminal owns native scrollback.\r\n\r\nUse \u001b[0m--tmux\u001b[38;5;45m at launch. \u001b[0mtctl\u001b[38;5;45m wraps the command in tmux, starts tmux with \u001b[0mTERM=xterm-256color\u001b[38;5;45m, and preconfigures \u001b[0mdefault-terminal=tmux-256color\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0mterminal-features=...,xterm-256color:RGB\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0mterminal-overrides=...,xterm-256color:Tc\u001b[38;5;45m (fallback for tmux < 3.2), \u001b[0mCOLORTERM=truecolor\u001b[38;5;45m (via \u001b[0mset-environment\u001b[38;5;45m), \u001b[0mescape-time=50\u001b[38;5;45m, and \u001b[0mmode-keys=vi\u001b[38;5;45m.\r\n\r\nCopy-mode: \u001b[0mctrl-b [\u001b[38;5;45m to enter, \u001b[0mg g\u001b[38;5;45m top, \u001b[0mshift-g\u001b[38;5;45m bottom, \u001b[0mctrl-u\u001b[38;5;45m/\u001b[0mctrl-d\u001b[38;5;45m half-page, \u001b[0m/\u001b[38;5;45m search, \u001b[0mq\u001b[38;5;45m to exit (not \u001b[0mesc\u001b[38;5;45m).\r\n\r\nLaunch with tmux:\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\n$TCTL launch \"pi\" -s demo --backend tuistory --tmux \\\r\n  --repo-root /path/to/worktree \\\r\n  --cols 120 --rows 36 --record /tmp/demo.cast \\\r\n  --env FORCE_COLOR=3 --env COLORTERM=truecolor\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\nWhen recording includes tmux redraws, asciinema must wrap tmux, not the reverse.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mKnown dead ends\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n • **Raw \u001b[0masciinema rec\u001b[38;5;45m**: Do not call \u001b[0masciinema rec\u001b[38;5;45m directly. \u001b[0mtctl --record\u001b[38;5;45m wraps \u001b[0masciinema rec\u001b[38;5;45m around the PTY so that tuistory-relay still owns the session and interactive TUIs (Ink/React) receive stdin correctly. Calling \u001b[0masciinema rec\u001b[38;5;45m manually bypasses this wiring — stdin forwarding breaks, typed keys echo on the outer PTY instead of reaching the child, and tuistory commands (\u001b[0mwait\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0msnapshot\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0mclose\u001b[38;5;45m) cannot find the session.\r\n • **Raw \u001b[0mtuistory launch\u001b[38;5;45m with tctl flags**: \u001b[0mtuistory\u001b[38;5;45m has no \u001b[0m--record\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--backend\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--repo-root\u001b[38;5;45m, or \u001b[0m--env\u001b[38;5;45m flags. Passing them crashes \u001b[0mtuistory-relay\u001b[38;5;45m. Use \u001b[0mtctl\u001b[38;5;45m for all launches.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mRecovery\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\n$TCTL -s demo press esc         # bail out of a stuck dialog\r\n$TCTL -s demo snapshot --trim   # check visible state\r\n$TCTL -s demo close             # hard reset\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;39mEscape hatch: raw tuistory (last resort)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nIf \u001b[0mtctl\u001b[38;5;45m itself is broken or unavailable, you can fall back to raw \u001b[0mtuistory\u001b[38;5;45m for non-recording sessions only. Raw \u001b[0mtuistory\u001b[38;5;45m accepts only \u001b[0m--cols\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--rows\u001b[38;5;45m, and \u001b[0m-s\u001b[38;5;45m — no other flags. Do not pass \u001b[0m--record\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--backend\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--repo-root\u001b[38;5;45m, \u001b[0m--env\u001b[38;5;45m, or \u001b[0m--tmux\u001b[38;5;45m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[0m`\u001b[38;5;45mbash\r\ntuistory launch \"my-tui-app\" -s demo --cols 120 --rows 36\r\ntuistory -s demo wait \">\" --timeout 15000\r\ntuistory -s demo snapshot --trim\r\ntuistory -s demo close\r\n\u001b[0m``\r\n\r\n"]
